Z||000000||Rhpetterson||03-11-2001||09:10 AM||||What is the cheapest way to get power out of my v6   I had a 4cyl saturn sc2 before and it had more power than my v6  i know the exaust manifold gaskets need to be replaced so i figured i would put better manifolds on it... any suggestions??||||reg||5
Z||000001||Seanh||03-11-2001||09:32 AM||||Keep the stock manifolds and have them ported out. It only costs like $100 or somthing. I would have the joints welded also when the out of the car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||03-11-2001||12:15 PM||||I will second that good advise.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||03-11-2001||12:34 PM||||If you got a compressor and a small air grinder you could port the manifolds yourself and save the $100 for something else.  When I had my V6 in my car I did it in about an hour and a half.  You could also use a drill with a grinder attatchment but it'll take longer. Definately start with the manifolds!!<BR>High flow cat and muffler?||||reg||1
