Z||000011||Standard||03-12-2001||12:46 AM||||Stick with having the stock manifolds ported.  If you go to headers on a fairly stock engine you'll lose torque and shift the powerband higher.  Not really good for a street driven car.||||reg||1
Z||000012||1FST2M6||03-12-2001||08:42 AM||||ok.. i'm NOT gunna say don't buy those headers... but look here..<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno.jpg</A> <P>the loss of 11blft through most of the theuseable RPM range was NOT worth the $522. porting the stock manifolds is the way to go. you can do it with a dremel also. ditch the stock exhaust and replace it with 2.5" piping and muffler.. for the best performance a single in single out 2.5 muffler is the way to go. yeah you'll only have one tip.. but you'll be faster/ stronger /better and you'll have $ in your pocket over the header install.<P><BR>oh as for what Archie says.. HELL YEAH do it! <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Wade87GT||03-12-2001||09:40 AM||||1FST2M6,<BR>You're saying use 2.5" pipes from the y-pipe back? Or fab a 2.5" y-pipe also to go with the rest of the system?<P>Wade<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000014||c m west||03-12-2001||11:22 AM||||Archie, I am simply attempting to make people aware that there are products out there that are designed SPECIFICLY for a stock Fiero, not a Fiero that utilizes a motor that was never structuraly designed to be in a Fiero - such as a small block<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000015||1FST2M6||03-12-2001||11:27 AM||||from the stock Y-pipe back a 2.5" system has made the best HP and TQ numbers for us.. we've tried Stock, Ocelot, 2.5x2.25 camaro flowmaster , 2.5" flowmaster and the current 2.5" brullen. the 2.5 makes the best hp numbers and hold the torque curve close to stock.. the 2.25" resonated like CRAZY in the cabin and had a hiccup at 3500-4200. (dip in HP)<P>-----<BR>uum ... they weren't designed to have TDCs or 3.8 S/Cs either...  to each his own... and the long tube headers aren't optimal for a stock Fiero. they shift the curves up in the RPMs to far killing the low end torque and harming my 0-60 times. under nitrous they kick some serious @$$ but there are only a handfull nitrous runners out there.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6headerdyno.jpg</A>  <BR>that much of a torque loss isn't worth the 7hp gain at 5200.<P>but on the other hand i did gain 61lbft on nitrous.. with NO jet change. from 253 to 309.7. theres a trade off for everything. <P>we have proof that the V8 only adds like 140lbs to the chassis... what does a 3.8 s/c tip the scales at? also, Please note C West now has headers for a V8. hummm... <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Nashco||03-12-2001||06:37 PM||||I knew that I wasn't the only one getting tired of the daily barrage of obvious advertising.<P>CM, we know you have these products, but you could contribute a little information without selling something.  Also note, not everyone is looking to buy some super-duper stuff for the price of their right arm.  Note he said the "cheapest way" to get power, not the latest high-tech computer tuned stuff.<P>I'm not trying to be rude about this, but you should try to lay off the salesmanship a little.  Even if you contributed outside of selling stuff that would be an improvement.  Consider your image; doesn't it bother you when your favorite show has too many ads in it?  After a while you don't even pay attention.<P>Thanks for taking this into consideration, rather than immediately shooting a reply back to the list.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 03-12-2001).]||||reg||1
